   "mark": "quay",
   "id": "quay_view",
   "say": "The quay is timber piles and packed gravel, and the mud under the water is full of broken amphorae: generations of them, dropped, cracked, emptied and thrown in. A barge from downriver is unloading wine. Another, empty, waits with its lines slack, and the boatmen keep looking south."
